  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para>Use the following information to answer questions 1 - 5. </para>
<blockquote>
  The temperature was recorded at several times during the day. Function \(T\) gives the temperature in degrees Fahrenheit, \(n\) hours since midnight. A graph for this function is provided.
</blockquote>
<para><figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/628c3b7693e07969ceb66d4d1b9c3ed03f8a0fd9"/></media></figure></para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="3e66f7ed-a847-45ef-ba68-6f612a0510e3" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
  <!-- Question 1 -->
  <exercise data-content-id="36fb9833-9b22-48d3-ba94-bfb28c0d0c2e" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="2" data-solution="negative" data-solution-options="[&quot;positive&quot;, &quot;negative&quot;, &quot;zero&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>For the interval from \(n = 1\) to \(n = 5\), determine if the average rate of change of the temperature is positive, negative, or zero.</para>
      </problem>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try Again. Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.1 - 4.8.4. </para>
    </div>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Negative</para>
    </solution>
  </exercise>
  <!-- Question 2 -->
  <exercise data-content-id="17ce8bbf-5675-409a-988f-8f28ec382260" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="2" data-solution="positive" data-solution-options="[&quot;positive&quot;, &quot;negative&quot;, &quot;zero&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>For the interval from \(n = 5\) to \(n = 7\), determine if the average rate of change of the temperature is positive, negative, or zero.</para>
      </problem>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try Again. Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.1 - 4.8.4.</para>
    </div>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Positive</para>
    </solution>
  </exercise>
  <!-- Question 3 -->
  <exercise data-content-id="d64e57ef-2350-47f5-a377-889332659ba1" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="2" data-solution="positive" data-solution-options="[&quot;positive&quot;, &quot;negative&quot;, &quot;zero&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>For the interval from \(n = 10\) to \(n = 20\), determine if the average rate of change of the temperature is positive, negative, or zero.</para>
      </problem>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try Again. Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.1 - 4.8.4.</para>
    </div>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Positive</para>
    </solution>
  </exercise>
  <!-- Question 4 -->
  <exercise data-content-id="95188503-775f-411f-891e-da2d26468ed6" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="2" data-solution="zero" data-solution-options="[&quot;positive&quot;, &quot;negative&quot;, &quot;zero&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>For the interval from \(n = 15\) to \(n = 18\), determine if the average rate of change of the temperature is positive, negative, or zero.</para>
      </problem>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try Again. Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.1 - 4.8.4.</para>
    </div>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Zero</para>
    </solution>
  </exercise>
  <!-- Question 5 -->
  <exercise data-content-id="9f6200ba-6973-4e97-b2d9-676e4d513843" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="2" data-solution="negative" data-solution-options="[&quot;positive&quot;, &quot;negative&quot;, &quot;zero&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>For the interval from \(n = 20\) to \(n = 24\), determine if the average rate of change of the temperature is positive, negative, or zero.</para>
      </problem>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try Again. Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.1 - 4.8.4.</para>
    </div>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Negative</para>
    </solution>
  </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> </div>
</div>
<para>The graph below shows the total distance, in feet, walked by a person as a function of time, in seconds. Use this information to answer questions 6 - 7.</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Distance Graph"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/dbec756aaee450163ee36c17b0b92acc17a32b69"/></media></figure></para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="66e8867e-e915-45e8-b93a-014d4a722720" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!-- Question 6 -->
  <exercise data-content-id="5cfaa9e4-f352-4656-b90d-04385efdf1c0" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="2" data-solution="Between 80 and 100 seconds" data-solution-options="[&quot;Between 0 and 40 seconds&quot;, &quot;Between 20 and 40 seconds&quot;, &quot;Between 80 and 100 seconds&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Given the graph of total distance walked as a function of time, was the person walking faster between 20 and 40 seconds or between 80 and 100 seconds?</para>
      </problem>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try Again. Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.1 - 4.8.4.</para>
    </div>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Between 80 and 100 seconds</para>
    </solution>
  </exercise>
  <!-- Question 7 -->
  <exercise data-content-id="a8564426-ea5c-4301-b4ef-b89e94193f78" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="2" data-solution="Between 0 and 40 seconds" data-solution-options="[&quot;Between 0 and 40 seconds&quot;, &quot;Between 40 and 80 seconds&quot;, &quot;Between 40 and 100 seconds&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Was the person walking faster between 0 and 40 seconds or between 40 and 100 seconds, based on the given graph?</para>
      </problem>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try Again. Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.1 - 4.8.4.</para>
    </div>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Between 0 and 40 seconds</para>
    </solution>
  </exercise>
  <para>Use the following information to answer questions 8 - 11.</para>
  <blockquote>
    The height, in feet, of a squirrel running up and down a tree is a function of time, in seconds.
  </blockquote>
  <para>Match each description with a statement about the average rate of change of the function for that interval.</para>
  <!--Q8 -->
  <exercise data-content-id="9b6b5602-f18c-4172-b78e-dabe92a3384e" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="Large and positive" data-solution-options="[&quot;Negative&quot;, &quot;Zero&quot;, &quot;Small and positive&quot;, &quot;Large and positive&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>For questions 8 - 11, use the following scenario. </para>
      <blockquote>
      <para>The height, in feet, of a squirrel running up and down a tree is a function of time, in seconds.</para>
      </blockquote>
        <para>Match each description with a statement about the average rate of change of the function for that interval.</para>
      
      <para>The squirrel runs up the tree very fast. The average rate of change is - </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The average rate of change is large and positive.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.1 - 4.8.5.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q3b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="53a323b9-b7d1-4a6a-a5b0-cb5ad212906a" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="Zero" data-solution-options="[&quot;Negative&quot;, &quot;Zero&quot;, &quot;Small and positive&quot;, &quot;Large and positive&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>The squirrel starts and ends at the same height. The average rate of change is - </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The average rate of change is zero.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.1 - 4.8.5. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q3c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="ab53564e-2bb2-4af8-bf28-151d03a9cfb4" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="Negative" data-solution-options="[&quot;Negative&quot;, &quot;Zero&quot;, &quot;Small and positive&quot;, &quot;Large and positive&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>The squirrel runs down the tree. The average rate of change is _____. </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!The average rate of change is negative.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.1 - 4.8.5. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q3d-->
  <exercise data-content-id="441417cc-6a8a-401e-b12f-52bfcbc23d0d" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="Small and positive" data-solution-options="[&quot;Negative&quot;, &quot;Zero&quot;, &quot;Small and positive&quot;, &quot;Large and positive&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>The squirrel runs up the tree slowly. The average rate of change is _____. </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.1 - 4.8.5. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q 12 -->
  <exercise data-content-id="d47c6530-0e2a-4c55-97e4-ce0e632f01f7" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="-1.025 percent per year" data-solution-options="[&quot;1.025 percent per year&quot;, &quot;-1.025 percent per year&quot;, &quot;0.35 percent per year&quot;, &quot;-2.4 percent per year&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>The percentage of voters ages 18 to 29 who participated in each United States presidential election between the years 1988 and 2016 is shown in the table.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
        <thead/>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">
              Year
            </entry>
            <entry>
              1988
            </entry>
            <entry>
              1992
            </entry>
            <entry>
              1996
            </entry>
            <entry>
              2000
            </entry>
            <entry>
              2004
            </entry>
            <entry>
              2008
            </entry>
            <entry>
              2012
            </entry>
            <entry>
              2016
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">
              Percentage of voters ages 18–29
            </entry>
            <entry>
              35.7
            </entry>
            <entry>
              42.7
            </entry>
            <entry>
              33.1
            </entry>
            <entry>
              34.5
            </entry>
            <entry>
              45.0
            </entry>
            <entry>
              48.4
            </entry>
            <entry>
              40.9
            </entry>
            <entry>
              43.4
            </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <para>The function \(P\) gives the percent of voters ages 18 to 29 years old who participated in the election in year \(t\).</para>
      <para>Determine the average rate of change for \(P\) between 1992 and 2000.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!  -1.025 percent per year </para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities  4.8.1 - 4.8.5. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="6c3fd095-c018-4f05-a8fb-49b8fc6bce96" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(\frac25\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;2&quot;, &quot;\\(\\frac25\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(-\\frac25\\)&quot;, &quot;6&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Some points from a linear function, \(f(x)\), are listed in the table below. What is the rate of change of this linear function?</para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
        <thead/>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">
              \(x\)
            </entry>
            <entry>
              0
            </entry>
            <entry>
              5
            </entry>
            <entry>
              10
            </entry>
            <entry>
              15
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">
              \(f(x)\)
            </entry>
            <entry>
              4
            </entry>
            <entry>
              6
            </entry>
            <entry>
              8
            </entry>
            <entry>
              10
            </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(\frac25\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="b792dc6a-15c9-4fce-a1c4-2b5ea3eff48a" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="-3">
    <problem>
      <para>Find the rate of change of the function, \(g(x)\), graphed below.</para>
      <para><figure><media alt="GRAPH OF A LINE THAT PASSES THROUGH THE POINTS (0, 2) AND (1, −1)."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/eeb492073a46c47fa8ff97bc8dcae77a0740168a"/></media></figure></para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.8.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--text input-->
  <exercise data-content-id="6fd19ceb-d534-44db-818a-3beafba2fdd0" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="4">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the rate of change of the function \(h(x)= 4x -7\)? </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
